Given \( k \in \mathbb{N} \) sparse sets \( S_1, S_2, \ldots, S_k \), we define the combined set \( S \) as follows:

\[ S = \{ \langle \text{encode}(i), x \rangle \mid x \in S_i, 1 \leq i \leq k \} \]

Where:
- \( \text{encode}(i) \) is the binary representation of the index \( i \) using \( \lceil \log_2 k \rceil \) bits.
- \( \langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle \) denotes concatenation of two strings.

