### Summary

The Turing Machine \( M \) operates efficiently in polynomial time by leveraging oracle access to the sparse set \( S_L \). This setup ensures a clear decision procedure for determining if \( x \) belongs to the language \( L \), utilizing the construction of \( S_L \) and the pre-defined mechanism within \(\textbf{P}_{angel}\).

